<%# One colour: a hex field that Coloris turns into a swatch button and a
    picker, with the palette offered as swatches.

    The text field is the whole contract. It posts #rrggbb, or '' for no
    colour, and without JavaScript it is still a working hex field — Coloris
    only adds the swatch and the popover on top. What the picker offers and how
    it is labelled comes from the page's data-ea-coloris attribute, read by
    expert_agile_colors.js, so nothing here is inline script.

    Locals: name (form field name), id (unique per field), selected (stored
    hex or nil), group_label (what this is the colour of). %>
<span class="ea-color-field">
  <%= text_field_tag name, selected,
                     :id => id,
                     :class => 'ea-color-input',
                     :maxlength => 7,
                     :size => 9,
                     :placeholder => l(:label_none),
                     :pattern => '#?[0-9a-fA-F]{3}([0-9a-fA-F]{3})?',
                     :autocomplete => 'off',
                     :spellcheck => 'false',
                     :'aria-label' => "#{l(:label_expert_agile_color)}: #{group_label}" %>
</span>
